-- title:
--   Descent of extra-level e_γ-stability from ̄ k to k₀
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r \neq r$, and $N$ is a nonzero natural number, squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$.
--
--   **Coefficients.** $\mathcal{O}$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ is irreducible, $\mathcal{O}$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, the residue ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. Next, $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to: completeness for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), maximality of that ideal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ (`hFr`). Thus $k_0 := O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ is a field. Finally $v_{\det} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) is a monoid homomorphism with $v_{\det}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli frame.** $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite ($0 < a$ or $0 < b$) and is a division algebra at exactly the places above $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), with $\Lambda$ a maximal order. The pair $(\mathcal{X}, f)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ with the point map `pt` is a coarse moduli scheme for fake elliptic curves of level $N$ for $\Lambda$ (`h𝒳`: isomorphism-invariance, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points, universality). An auxiliary level $n \geq 3$ is prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and coprime to $N$; $(M, f_M, \mathrm{pt}_F)$ is a fine moduli scheme for fake elliptic curves with full level $n$ (`hM`), and $\rho : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$, $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ is a level-twisting action of a group $G$ (`hρ`: $\rho$ acts over the base, twisting a full level structure by $\chi(g)$ moves the moduli point by $\rho(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$). The morphism $p : M \to \mathcal{X}$ lies over the base (`hp`), is invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`), and carries the fine moduli point of $(E,P)$ to the coarse point of $E$ (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, $(\mathcal{Y}_\ell, g_\ell, \mathrm{pt}_T)$ is a coarse moduli scheme for fake elliptic curves with an extra level structure at $\ell$ (`h𝒴`); the two degeneracy morphisms $d_0^\ell, d_1^\ell : \mathcal{Y}_\ell \to \mathcal{X}$ lie over the base and realise, on points, forgetting the extra level (`hd₀`) and passing to the quotient by it along a level isogeny (`hd₁`); $a_r, a_{\bar r} : \mathcal{X}\to\mathcal{X}$ lie over the base and realise the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side and the group $\tilde\Gamma$.** $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ is definite ($a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$) and a division algebra exactly at the places above $\bar r$ (`hdef`); $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1 \leq \Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$, $n_1$ an adelic unit in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$, and $R_1 \cap R_1^{n_1}$ an Eichler order of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); $\iota_0 : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$ is an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map, and $v$ is the height-one prime of $\mathbb{Z}$ containing $r$. The subgroup $\Gamma_t$ consists exactly of the units integral away from $v$ with respect to $R_1$ (`hΓt`). Global elements $s_\ell$ and adelic elements $s^f_\ell$ are given for each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, with: the components of $s^f_\ell$ away from $r$ equal to $s_\ell$, its component above $r$ equal to $1$, the element $\ell \cdot (s^f_\ell)^{-1}$ lying in the level Hecke set of $(\Lambda_1, R_1 \cap R_1^{n_1})$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1 \cap R_1^{n_1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\operatorname{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$ (`hs`); and $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). The unit $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **The base point over $k_0$.** All integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and `coord` is an order coordinate system $\Lambda \to \mathbb{W}(\mathbb{F}_{r^2})^2$ (additive, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, with the Frobenius-twisted product rule, injective, with dense image, and trace-compatible). $A_0$ is a fake elliptic curve of level $N$ over $k_0$, $X_0$ a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $k_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), $\theta_0$ a system of formal coordinates in two variables for $A_0$ with $A_0$ a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`), together with families $e, e' : \Gamma_t \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base and degrees `deg`. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (summarised here) require: each $(e_\gamma, e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level-$N$ structure; $e$ is multiplicative and sends rational scalars to multiplications, in both cases up to powers of $r$, and conversely only scalars $\gamma$ give multiplications; for every injective embedding of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ through which each $e_\gamma$ is induced, on formal coordinates, by an endomorphism $\varepsilon$ of $X_0$ with $E_0\varepsilon = r^{k_\gamma}\, g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; each full level $n$ structure on $A_0$ gets a labelling $\Gamma_t \to \Lambda$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$, describing the action of $e_\gamma$ on it; and over every algebraically closed $k_0$-algebra, every level-preserving self-isogeny pair of $r$-power degree of a pullback of $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to $r$-powers. The order $R_2 \leq R_1$ with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) carries $\hat e : R_2 \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base, and `hE5a`–`hE5e` (summarised here) require that $\hat e$ be additive on points, commute with the $\Lambda$-action, preserve the level, be multiplicative and unital, agree with the $\Lambda$-action on integers, satisfy $\hat e_{\bar x}\hat e_x = [\operatorname{nrd} x]$, agree up to $r$-powers with $e_\gamma$ when $x = r^{k}\gamma$, and be jointly rationalised with $e$ by a single $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$.
--
--   **Formal side.** $\iota : \mathbb{W}(\mathbb{F}_{r^2}) \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a ring map, $\Phi$ is a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ that is special for the reduction of $\iota$ and of height $4$, and $MD$ is a moduli package which is a Zariski sheaf, with a classifying map $\eta$ from rigidified objects of $\Phi$; `hη` asserts that over noetherian base rings $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is natural, and is surjective after a Zariski cover by localisations. $E_0$ embeds the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ injectively, with image commensurable to the integral matrices in the precise sense of `hE₀`. The data $e_D$ with `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD` give, over noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebras in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, a natural bijection of the functor of $G$-points of $MD$ with the product of the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-points functor and Deligne's functor $\Omega$, compatible with the leg, converting the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $G$-points into the $v_{\det}$-twisted action on $\Omega$, converting $\pi$-translation into the Frobenius twist of the leg, and with $\pi$-translates always existing. Further, $\kappa : k_0 \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ is compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ and the comparison $\Xi$.** $P_0$ is a full level $n$ structure on $A_0$; $A_{0w}$, $a_w, a'_w, b_w, b'_w$, $k_w$ realise $A_{0w}$ as the $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ (`hALw`) together with a level-preserving isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ back to $A_0$ (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw` rationalises simultaneously all $e_\gamma$ and the composite $a_w$ followed by $b_w$, the latter matching $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to a power of $r$. The map $\Xi$ sends a rigidified curve over a noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent to a $G$-point of $MD$; `hΞleg`, `hΞnat`, `hΞiso`, `hΞdef` assert that its leg is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$ when $B$ has no nontrivial idempotents, that it is natural under pullback, that it is unchanged by isomorphisms of rigidified curves in the stated comparison sense, and that it is computed by $\eta$ applied to a rigidified object obtained by transport along $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ with shift $j \leq 1$.
--
--   **Transport hypotheses.** For a fixed $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$: `heqΓ` and `heqW` state that translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$, respectively passing to the $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner quotient in the stated comparison sense, corresponds under $\Xi$ to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$, respectively $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$, for some $c \in \mathbb{Z}$. The hypotheses `hK1`–`hK4` state that the relation "$\Xi\langle E,\varrho\rangle$ has leg the $(-v_{\det}(g_0))$-twist of $\psi$ and $e_D$ of it is $g_0^{-1}$-twisted-equivalent to $(\psi,P)$" is surjective in $(\psi,P)$, determines $(E,\varrho)$ up to isomorphism in the stated comparison sense, lifts along morphisms of base rings, and lifts along surjections with square-zero-type kernels. The hypotheses `hC0e`, `hC0u` give existence and uniqueness of the norm-level transport of $P_0$ to a full level $n$ structure; $\Theta_f$ with `hnat`, `hG`, `hC2`, `hC2c` is a natural transformation to the nilpotent points of $f_M$, equivariant for $\rho$ and compatible with the fine and coarse moduli points; and $\theta_t : \Gamma_t \to G$ with `hC3` (several clauses, summarised here) transports the $\iota_0(\gamma)$-twisted action to a change of rigidification, with the level structure moved by $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$, and with extra-level structures at primes $\ell \neq r$ invertible in the base detected through the rigidification.
--
--   **The situation considered.** $k$ is an algebraically closed field and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hk`), $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to k$ is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map, $P, P'$ are Deligne data over $k$, and $E, E'$ are fake elliptic curves over $k$ with rigidifications $\varrho, \varrho'$ relative to $A_0$ and the leg twisted by $-v_{\det}(g_0)$; `hΞψ`, `hev` and `hΞψ'`, `hev'` assert that $\Xi\langle E,\varrho\rangle$ and $\Xi\langle E',\varrho'\rangle$ have the prescribed leg and correspond under $e_D$, after the $g_0^{-1}$-twist, to $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$. Moreover $i : E.A \cong E'.A$ is an isomorphism over the base compatible with the group law, the $\Lambda$-action and the level-$N$ structure (`hvia`). Finally $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$, $\varrho''$ is a further rigidification of $E$ with the same prescribed leg and corresponding to $(\psi,P')$ (`hev''`), the pair $(\psi,P)$ is carried to $(\psi,P')$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ (`htw`), $\varrho''$ is the translate of $\varrho$ by $e_\gamma$ in the sense of `IsTranslateBy` (`htr`), and `hcorr` provides the comparison between $\varrho''$ and $\varrho'$ along $i$: morphisms $i_b$, $u_A$ on the reductions and on the $A_0$-legs, compatible with the structure morphisms and with $i$, such that $i_b$ followed by $\varrho'.\varphi$, $u_A$ and multiplication by $r^{i_1}$ equals $\varrho''.\varphi$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j_1}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every prime $\ell \neq r$ whose image in $k$ is a unit, and every extra level structure $K_0$ at $\ell$ on $A_0$ (the bound name $K_0$ here denotes such a structure, not the fraction field), the following implication holds. Suppose that for every scheme $T$, every pair of morphisms $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k_0$ and $t' : T \to \operatorname{Spec}(k/\pi k)$ such that $t'$ followed by the morphism induced by the residue leg of the $(-v_{\det}(g_0))$-twist of $\psi$ equals $t$, and every point $R$ of $A_0$ over $t$: if $R$ factors through the closed immersion $K_0 \to A_0.A$, then so does $R$ followed by $e_\gamma$. Then the same stability holds without any constraint on the base: for every scheme $T$, every $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k_0$ and every point $R$ of $A_0$ over $t$, if $R$ factors through $K_0 \to A_0.A$ then $R$ followed by $e_\gamma$ factors through $K_0 \to A_0.A$.
--
--   In the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$, the matching of the $\Gamma_t$-action with the twisted action on Deligne's functor requires comparing extra level structures at auxiliary primes $\ell \neq r$; this step isolates the descent part of that comparison, passing from stability of an extra level under the self-isogeny $e_\gamma$ of the base point $A_0$ tested on schemes over the residue field of $k$ to stability tested on all schemes over $k_0 = O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$. It is the second half of a two-step cut of the statement that combines the extra-level detection criterion with the determinant normalisation, and is used there.
